Day 08 – Dockerfile and Custom Docker Image

Objective

Learn how to create a custom Docker image using a Dockerfile and run a website container from that image.

Dockerfile Instructions Covered

- FROM: Defines the base image.
- COPY: Copies project files into the image.
- RUN: Executes commands during image build.
- CMD: Defines the default command when a container starts.

Dockerfile Created

FROM nginx:latest
COPY . /usr/share/nginx/html/

Hands-on Implementation

1. Created a Dockerfile inside the website project directory.
2. Used the official Nginx image as the base image.
3. Copied website files into the Nginx document root.
4. Built a custom Docker image:

sudo docker build -t aman-nginx:v1 .

5. Verified the custom image:

sudo docker images

6. Created and started a container using the custom image:

sudo docker run -d --name aman-website -p 8080:80 aman-nginx:v1

7. Verified the running container using:

sudo docker ps

8. Opened the website in the browser and confirmed that it was accessible.

Key Learning

- Difference between Dockerfile, Docker image, and Docker container.
- Purpose of FROM, COPY, RUN, and CMD.
- How to build a custom Docker image.
- How to run a container using a custom image.
- How to verify a running container.

Status

Completed the Dockerfile creation, custom image build, and container deployment hands-on practice.
